.TH ISHTARIA-ADMIN 1 "2026" "ishtaria-admin" "Ishtaria"
.SH NAME
ishtaria-admin \- text-mode administration of an Ishtaria world server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ishtaria-admin
[\fB\-\-database\-url=\fIURL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turbo Vision interface for the server operator: save, load, rename, delete and
export world maps; rename, ban and delete players; manage portals to linked
worlds; start the server service; schedule a server shutdown with a notice
shown to players. At start-up it reports the service state, the address the
server listens on and the datadisks the world was generated with, and offers
to generate a first world map or start a stopped service.
.PP
It talks directly to the PostgreSQL database of ishtaria-server. Run it as the
service user: \fBsudo \-u ishtaria ishtaria\-admin\fR. Started as root without an
explicit URL it switches to that user itself. Starting the unit needs root
privileges or a polkit rule for the ishtaria user.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DATABASE_URL
Connection string. Default: postgresql:///ishtaria?host=/var/run/postgresql
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SERVER_CONFIG
Server configuration to read the listen address from.
Default: /etc/ishtaria/server.toml
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_SERVER
Alternative ishtaria-server binary (datadisk helpers).
.TP
.B ISHTARIA_WORLDGEN
Alternative ishtaria-worldgen binary (map generation).
